1
00:00:01,719 --> 00:00:06,899
Lunchtime food vendor Thadeus Suggs has no
trouble taking an order from deaf customers

2
00:00:06,899 --> 00:00:10,310
at this store in Washington's Union Market.

3
00:00:10,310 --> 00:00:15,810
Communication is easy because the 23-year-old
cook is fluent in American Sign Language.

4
00:00:15,810 --> 00:00:22,689
Suggs, who also is deaf, began working at
the market soon after it opened last year.

5
00:00:22,689 --> 00:00:26,640
That's when he took a break from studying
across the street at Gallaudet University

6
00:00:26,640 --> 00:00:33,090
-- the only one in the world designed to accomodate
Deaf and hard of hearing students.

7
00:00:33,090 --> 00:00:37,870
With the help of Gallaudet interpreter Carolyn
Ressler, Suggs explains what he likes about

8
00:00:37,870 --> 00:00:38,870
his job.

9
00:00:38,870 --> 00:00:43,320
"One nice thing is it's so close to Gallaudet,
which by the way is the 'Deaf Mecca.'

10
00:00:43,320 --> 00:00:50,350
And with that, we are providing services to
the Gallaudet community as well as the community

11
00:00:50,350 --> 00:00:51,350
at large."

12
00:00:51,350 --> 00:00:57,310
Suggs can read lips and interact with people
verbally, as well.

13
00:00:57,310 --> 00:01:03,190
His boss at the TaKorean store, Ross Mayhood,
says that makes Suggs a well-rounded communicator.

14
00:01:03,190 --> 00:01:07,080
"He is probably the most valuable member of
our staff.

15
00:01:07,080 --> 00:01:12,100
And he has probably been a big part of how
popular we are with the Gallaudet crew."

16
00:01:12,100 --> 00:01:13,830
Suggs is not alone.

17
00:01:13,830 --> 00:01:17,920
Deaf employees make up about 10 percent of
the market's workforce.

18
00:01:17,920 --> 00:01:21,640
They also attract regular customers like Cary
Barbin.

19
00:01:21,640 --> 00:01:25,280
"I love the fact that this is a sign language
environment.

20
00:01:25,280 --> 00:01:29,680
Many of the employees sign, so I can order
my food in American Sign Language."

21
00:01:29,680 --> 00:01:34,300
Another attraction for the deaf community
is the market's user-friendly layout.

22
00:01:34,300 --> 00:01:39,060
Gallaudet planning director Hansel Bauman
encouraged the developer to build a "deaf

23
00:01:39,060 --> 00:01:42,100
space" that is sensitive to deaf people's
needs.

24
00:01:42,100 --> 00:01:48,360
"In terms of visual language, to be able to
see one another and communicate clearly while

25
00:01:48,360 --> 00:01:49,590
you're walking.

26
00:01:49,590 --> 00:01:51,750
What that means is, you're not looking at
the path forward.

27
00:01:51,750 --> 00:01:53,570
So you need a little bit more room."

28
00:01:53,570 --> 00:01:59,100
"Union Market has tried to incorporate several
aspects of deaf space into its design.

29
00:01:59,100 --> 00:02:04,260
There's lots of light, all the vendors are
in one big room, and the aisles between them

30
00:02:04,260 --> 00:02:08,170
are wider than you would find in a typical
store."

31
00:02:08,170 --> 00:02:13,220
Developer Steve Boyle of EDENS says those
features also have a broader objective.

32
00:02:13,220 --> 00:02:18,040
"The market itself really was meant to be
an anchor for the community.

33
00:02:18,040 --> 00:02:24,610
It wasn't truly designed around deaf design
principles, simply because we don't really

34
00:02:24,610 --> 00:02:27,730
understand them the way we need to -- yet."

35
00:02:27,730 --> 00:02:33,120
Alena Francis, another deaf employee, says
dealing with some customers can be challenging.

36
00:02:33,120 --> 00:02:37,110
"When they find out that I'm deaf, it kind
of throws them off a little bit.

37
00:02:37,110 --> 00:02:40,300
And sometimes people react very harshly and
it's kind of hard.

38
00:02:40,300 --> 00:02:42,480
They'll ignore me and just walk away."

39
00:02:42,480 --> 00:02:46,069
But Suggs says the market also promotes understanding.

40
00:02:46,069 --> 00:02:52,849
"I'm really happy that this was established
as a business, because you know once again,

41
00:02:52,849 --> 00:02:56,180
it's another place where deaf and hearing
people can come together and just kind of

42
00:02:56,180 --> 00:02:57,349
hang out and live together."

43
00:02:57,349 --> 00:02:58,370
[Suggs] "Enjoy!"

44
00:02:58,370 --> 00:02:59,920
[Male customer] "Thanks."

45
00:02:59,920 --> 00:03:02,060
Michael Lipin, VOA News, Washington

